---
// The Switch page, switching accounts round 2 (the switch UX sketch), in place of the profile's settings as in the app.
// NOW is the account in use, lit; under TO every standby account, most room first, the picked one lit in mint; the
// sessions are asked every time (nothing chosen for you); moving them always brings a backup, made right after the
// window closes; each sign-in is checked; Cancel stays in sight while it runs. The demo switches "work" (settings.astro
// runs it with sample timings, and shows the six cases it can meet when something goes wrong). Sample data only.
import { accounts, standby, byRoom, shortName } from "../data/demo";

const a = accounts.find((x) => x.id === "work")!;
const from = shortName(a.email);
const list = byRoom(standby.work);
---
<section class="sw-page" data-sw-page hidden aria-label="Switch account">
  <div class="sw-head"><h3 data-sw-head>Switch Claude {a.name} to <span class="tn">{shortName(list[0].email)}</span></h3></div>
  <!-- the line at the top while it runs, when it's done or when something went wrong: a display and the keys out -->
  <div class="sw-run" data-sw-run hidden></div>
  <!-- demo only: the cases a switch can meet when something goes wrong -->
  <div class="sw-demo" data-sw-demo><span class="sub">Demo: what can go wrong</span>
    <span class="switch small-switch" role="group" aria-label="What can go wrong">
      <button type="button" data-sw-fail="window">Window won't close</button><button type="button" data-sw-fail="half">Stopped half way</button><button type="button" data-sw-fail="wrong">Wrong account</button><button type="button" data-sw-fail="sidebar">Sidebar not reached</button><button type="button" data-sw-fail="cancel">Cancelled</button><button type="button" data-sw-fail="undo">Undo stopped</button>
    </span></div>
  <div class="sw-cols">
    <div class="sw-col">
      <div class="card"><h4>Accounts <i class="idot" title="The account the profile works on now, and the one to switch to, with their limits as cl_audit last read them. Under TO, every standby account, most room first: click one to pick it.">i</i></h4>
        <div class="acc-flow" data-sw-acc-flow></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Stays as it is <i class="idot" title="Switching changes only the account the profile works on. Everything that makes it the profile stays.">i</i></h4>
        <div class="srow"><span>Profile</span><span class="v-soft">Name, Dock icon, look</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Folder</span><span class="v-soft">{a.dir}: projects, settings, MCP, CLAUDE.md</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>History</span><span class="v-soft">Claude Code's, for claude --resume</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sw-col">
      <div class="card"><h4>Sessions <i class="idot" title="The Claude window's Code sessions: the sidebar's sessions, sections and groups, pins and scheduled tasks. If they move, the window opens the same on the other account. If they stay, each account keeps its own. Chats and Projects on claude.ai belong to each account and never move.">i</i></h4>
        <div class="srow"><span>Move them?</span><span class="switch small-switch" role="group" aria-label="Move the sessions?"><button type="button" data-sw-q="move">Move to <span class="tn">{shortName(list[0].email)}</span></button><button type="button" data-sw-q="leave">Leave with {from}</button></span></div>
        <p class="g-note sub" data-sw-qline>Choose one to go on: nothing is chosen for you.</p>
        <div class="srow"><span>Sessions</span><span class="v-soft">14 in the sidebar (and 3 archived)</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Sidebar</span><span class="v-soft">2 sections, 3 groups and the pins</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Routines</span><span class="v-soft">2 scheduled tasks</span></div>
        <p class="g-note sub">Chats and Projects on claude.ai don't move; they belong to each account.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" data-sw-backup><h4>Backup <i class="idot" title="Whenever the sessions move, cl_audit backs them up first, right after the window closes and before anything moves. Never in a backup: sign-ins, and the sidebar kept on claude.ai (the switch's own record puts that back). It's listed under the profile's Sessions until you delete it or it ages out.">i</i></h4>
        <div class="srow"><span>When</span><span class="v-soft" data-sw-bwhen>Every time the sessions move: right after the window closes, before anything moves</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>What</span><span class="v-soft">The window's Code-tab list for both accounts, scheduled tasks, its sidebar records; cl_audit's records</span></div>
        <div class="srow"><span>Takes</span><span class="v-soft">About 3 s, as clones: they share space with the originals</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card"><h4>Steps <i class="idot" title="What switching does, in order. Each step is checked before the next, each sign-in too. A receipt in cl_audit's folder keeps what moved: Cancel puts it back while the switch runs, and Undo after.">i</i></h4>
        <ol class="sw-steps" data-sw-steps></ol>
        <div class="sw-keys" data-sw-keys></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- the yes before it starts -->
  <div class="dialog-veil" data-sw-confirm hidden>
    <div class="dialog" role="alertdialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="sw-c-title">
      <b id="sw-c-title" data-sw-c-title></b>
      <p data-sw-c-text></p>
      <p class="sub">This is a demo, so nothing on your Mac changes.</p>
      <div class="dialog-btns sw-c-btns"><button type="button" class="pill small" data-sw-no>Cancel</button><button type="button" class="pill small tint t-green" data-sw-yes>Close and switch</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
